  {
   "id": "b3",
   "function": "explanation",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "In a petrol engine, air and fuel are already mixed when the spark arrives. The engineering lecture calls this a premixed flame. It spreads out from the spark through the ready mixture. The spark is just the starting signal. In the picture, the injector sits in the intake port.",
