  },
  {
   "id": "b4",
   "function": "explanation",
   "scene_type": "zlx_cutaway",
   "spoken": "In a diesel, the fuel is only injected into the hot, compressed air. It burns wherever it is mixing with air at that moment. The lecture compares this diffusion flame to a candle. There is no spark plug in this cylinder head at all.",
